# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Virtualenv
venv/
.venv/

# Secrets — never commit keys
.env
secrets.py

# Runtime output
logs/*.log
logs/*.jsonl

# Models are large; fetch them with scripts/, don't commit
assets/models/
*.onnx
*.gguf

# ...EXCEPT the wake word, which is Friday's name and cannot be re-downloaded.
# Every other model here is a fetch away (Piper voices, faster-whisper). This
# one was trained on this Pi by scripts/train_wake.py and exists nowhere else,
# so an SD card failure would take it with it. It is ~600 kB. Committing it is
# the difference between "re-run the trainer" and "it's gone".
# The room recording it trained against is NOT committed -- it is 45s of audio
# from Harsh's home and has no business in a repo.
!assets/models/wake/
!assets/models/wake/friday.onnx
# Harsh's own recordings of the wake word. ~40 short clips, ~2 MB. Committed
# because they are the ONE thing here that cannot be regenerated: Piper voices
# and whisper are a download away, the trained model is 25 minutes of CPU, and
# these are a person standing in a room saying a phrase forty times. Lose them
# and the only fix is to record them again.
!assets/models/wake/samples/
!assets/models/wake/samples/*.wav
# The 45s room recording stays out — it is ambient audio of Harsh's home and
# has no business in a repo.
assets/models/wake/ambient.wav
assets/models/wake/*.bak

# OS
.DS_Store

# runtime state (written by face_control.py)
state/*.txt
state/.emotion.*

# runtime state (written by app_control.py and the screen apps)
state/app_command.json
state/app_status.json
state/schedule.json
state/ring.wav
state/ring.json
state/.appcmd.*
state/.appstat.*
state/.sched.*
certs/
state/calibration.json
__pycache__/

# Arduino toolchain — 429 MB of downloaded compiler and cores. Vendored INSIDE
# the project (see tools/arduino-env.sh) so flashing needs no system package,
# but it is a build tool, not source, and must not be committed. The small
# env script and the sketch itself are.
tools/arduino/
tools/arduino-cli
tools/arduino-cli.tar.gz

# Runtime state, not source. The decision log is the record of what Friday DID
# on THIS robot -- it grows forever and means nothing in a fresh clone.
state/*.sqlite3
state/*.sqlite3-shm
state/*.sqlite3-wal
# Friday's memory is what it learned on THIS robot, in this room, from Harsh.
# It is personal and it means nothing in a fresh clone -- the schema is in
# memory.py and rebuilds itself on first use.
state/*.db
state/*.db-shm
state/*.db-wal
state/captures/

# arduino-cli's downloaded core and toolchain (~200 MB). The BINARY and the
# env script are tracked; what they fetch is not.
tools/arduino/
tools/arduino-cli
tools/arduino-cli.tar.gz

# Local repo bundles. A safety net against a corrupted .git, NOT an
# off-card backup -- an SD failure takes these with it. See README.
backup/

# The occupancy map of THIS room, rebuilt by slam/ every run. Runtime state,
# not source -- like state/*.db it means nothing in a fresh clone, and a stale
# one committed here would be silently loaded over a real survey.
state/map.npz

# ...AND the RL exploration policy, for the same reason as the wake word above.
# exploration_model.onnx is 144 kB, was trained on Harsh's laptop in a Gymnasium
# sim and scp'd here. It is the ONLY copy on this machine, and *.onnx above would
# silently drop it -- which is precisely how the last rebuild lost everything.
# The blackbox from the first autonomous run is committed with it: that CSV is
# the measured baseline (FRIDAY AUTONOMY BASELINE V1) every future run is
# compared against, and it cannot be re-recorded -- it was a specific 30 s in a
# specific room on 2026-08-28.
!rl/exploration_model.onnx

# rl/ runtime output: new black boxes are written per run and are NOT baseline.
rl/blackbox-*.csv
rl/state/

# The RL stack's own occupancy map, same reasoning as state/map.npz above: it is the
# survey of THIS room, rebuilt every run, and a stale one committed here would be
# silently loaded over a real one. Kept SEPARATE from map.npz on purpose -- that one
# is scan-matched (7.3 cm over 5.4 m), this one is dead-reckoned, and letting the
# worse estimate overwrite the better survey would destroy it without a word.
state/rl_map.npz
